<main id="main" class="wrap project-page"><a class="back-link" href="../index.html#projects">All projects</a><p class="eyebrow">Computer vision · 3D perception</p><h1>CenterPoint Joint Object–Attribute Prediction</h1><p class="lead">Extending a LiDAR-based 3D detector to jointly predict objects and attributes, including vehicle type and pedestrian posture.</p><div class="detail-result"><strong>83%</strong><span>average precision for vehicle and pedestrian object–attribute pairs</span></div><div class="prose"><p>This project extended the CenterPoint 3D detection model to predict object attributes alongside detections in autonomous driving LiDAR data.</p>
<h2>My contribution</h2><ul><li>Led the design and implementation of joint object and attribute prediction.</li><li>Managed data processing and augmented the nuScenes dataset with attribute labels.</li><li>Fine-tuned the model on both detection and attribute prediction objectives.</li></ul>
<h2>Results</h2><p>The model achieved 83% average precision for vehicle and pedestrian object–attribute pairs.</p>
